Chapter: GuardNestRt

 A `when` INSIDE a guard, inline rather than through a call: a called function
 has a scrutinee local of its own and cannot collide. `Boxed 5` is the case
 whose guard runs and is false, so the arm below must still see the Boxed
 record and not the inner scrutinee.

  Box =
    | Boxed (Integer)
    | Plain (Integer)

  classify : Box -> Integer
  classify (v) =
   when v
    is Boxed (x) when (when x is 7 -> True is otherwise -> False) -> 100
    is Boxed (y) -> 200 + y
    is Plain (z) -> 300 + z

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("boxed-7 " & show (classify (Boxed 7)))
   print-line-uni ("boxed-5 " & show (classify (Boxed 5)))
   print-line-uni ("plain-5 " & show (classify (Plain 5)))
  end
